# Line endings are part of this repository's content addressing.
#
# The task corpus, the freeze locks, and the per-task image locks all record
# SHA-256 hashes of files as they exist in the working tree
# (``vendored_tree_sha256``, ``freeze/grader_v1.lock.json`` protected_files,
# ``tasks/*/image.lock.json``). A CRLF checkout on Windows and an LF checkout on
# Linux therefore produce different hashes for byte-identical Git content, which
# makes every recorded hash platform-dependent.
#
# Default: normalize text to LF in the index and check it out as LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Hashed payloads: never apply any end-of-line conversion in either direction.
# The bytes stored in Git are exactly the bytes that get hashed and, for the
# vendored baselines, exactly the bytes mounted into the scoring container.
tasks/**            -text
tests/fixtures/**   -text
freeze/**           -text

# Patch fixtures are immutable, hashed evidence. Do not flag whitespace that is
# intentionally present in the payload under test.
*.patch -text -whitespace
